  <section>
    <p class="post-lead"><strong>Short answer:</strong> Telegram Premium users can use <strong>Star Messages</strong> to charge <strong>1-10,000 Stars</strong> for a message from anyone outside their contact list. It's turned on under <strong>Settings &gt; Privacy and Security &gt; Messages</strong>, you keep <strong>85%</strong> of what's paid, and you can refund a message with one tap even after reading it.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What is Star Messages, and why does it exist?</h2>
    <p>Star Messages is Telegram's feature for making incoming messages from strangers — people outside your contact list — cost something. It does two things at once: it protects popular or public-facing accounts from spam and unwanted messages, and it lets you earn a small amount from people who are genuinely willing to pay to reach you.</p>
    <p>It's different from a <a href="/en/blog/telegram-channel-subscription-stars">paid channel subscription</a> or a paid post — those monetize a channel's audience. Star Messages is about messages landing in your own personal chat or group.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who can actually use it?</h2>
    <p>In a private chat, only a <strong>Telegram Premium</strong> subscriber can turn this on. In groups it works differently: the group owner or an admin enables <strong>"Charge Stars for Messages"</strong> under the group's <strong>Permissions</strong> settings — no separate Premium subscription is required there, since the charge applies to the right to message the group itself.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to turn it on in a private chat</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Make sure you have Telegram Premium.</li>
      <li>Go to <strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <strong>Privacy and Security</strong> &gt; <strong>Messages</strong>.</li>
      <li>Turn on <strong>"Charge for messages."</strong></li>
      <li>Set a price between <strong>1 and 10,000 Stars</strong> per message.</li>
      <li>Optionally, add specific people or group members to an exception list who can message you for free.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How to turn it on in a group</h2>
    <p>The group owner or an admin opens the group's <strong>Permissions</strong> settings and enables <strong>"Charge Stars for Messages."</strong> This is a useful way to cut down on spam from strangers in large, open groups.</p>
  </section>

